<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">East Indies</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dutch East Indies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The East Indies is a historical term for the islands of South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, especially the Indonesian archipelago. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> East Indies formed the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a>, valued for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade">spices</a> and later plantation crops, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> occupied them during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> gained independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/east-indies.jpg" alt="East Indies" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jodocus Hondius I · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_East_Indies_by_Jodocus_Hondius_in_1606.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Dutch East Indies</b> were created when the Dutch state took over the Asian possessions of the bankrupt Dutch East India Company (VOC), whose charter expired at the end of 1799.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Act of Abjuration of 1581 renounced the sovereignty of Philip II, and within fourteen years Dutch merchants had sent the first expedition to the <b>East Indies</b> under Cornelis de Houtman (1595–1597).</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>By mid-1942, following the fall of Singapore in February, the conquest of the <b>Dutch East Indies</b>, and the extension of the Pacific perimeter to the Aleutian Islands, Japan controlled approximately seven million square kilometres.</blockquote><a href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Indonesia grew out of the <b>Dutch East Indies</b>, a colony assembled by the Netherlands over three centuries, and out of a nationalist movement that took shape in the early twentieth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/indonesia">Indonesia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In the <b>East Indies</b> the Dutch fleet under Karel Doorman was destroyed in the Battle of the Java Sea in February 1942 and the colony surrendered to Japan in March.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In the 19th century the Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1824 divided the region: the Dutch colonised the <b>East Indies</b> to the south, while the British held colonies and protectorates in the peninsula and Borneo to the north.</blockquote><a href="/language/malay">Malay · Speakers &amp; Spread</a></li></ul></section>
